The file has already been patched. The bug was on line 43:

```
if (foodSurplus >= 0) {
```

This meant population grew when `foodSurplus === 0` (break-even: production exactly equals consumption). The fix changes it to:

```
if (foodSurplus > 0) {
```

Population now only grows when there's an actual surplus (production > consumption), not when they're equal.


